A||||16||Raydar||'Scuse me while I whip this out! (Removed engine pics. Lots of 'em.) ||||1||
Z||000000||Raydar||11-16-2001||09:12 PM||||Okay, I bought this crunched Formula, September a year ago, for the drivetrain. Gonna transplant it into my 88 coupe. Been stripping it over the past few weeks. <I>Finally</I> dropped the cradle, today. <BR>By myself. Used two floor jacks, a bottle jack, four big concrete blocks and some pieces of 2x8. Rolled the cradle out on two side-by-side furniture dollies with 2x4s laid across them. Worked like a champ. And only had one stubborn cradle bolt. (Nothing that a 1/2 drive breaker bar and an impact socket couldn't handle.)<P>Here's the result, so far. <P>The donor. Would you believe I drove this into the garage under its own power? <BR>Actually sounds better than my daily driver.<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Wreck1.jpg">     <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap2_1.jpg">      <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap5.jpg">      <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap7.jpg">      <P>Nekkid engine compartment.<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/swap6.jpg">      <P>I'm trying to remove <I>anything</I> I might possibly need to make this thing work in my coupe. <P>The one remaining task is to remove the front suspension from the car and see if anything at all is salvageable. Then I'm going to have the hull hauled away. Hope I don't have to pay...<P>As I start the swap, I'll try to post pics.<P>If you are planning a swap like this, and have questions, please ask. I'll tell you all I can remember.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||11-16-2001||09:52 PM||||Looks good.  What all are you useing off that formula?  I may need some parts for my 88 coupe!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Like the mirrors.  Sounds like fun.  <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||11-16-2001||10:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Then I'm going to have the hull hauled away. Hope I don't have to pay...<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Let me know what you find out about this.  I will eventually have an 87GT skeleton to get rid of.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cheever_gold_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||11-16-2001||10:48 PM||||Nice job!  It must be great to haul that out without everything having a liberal coat of rust.  You should see mine.  And that's what a battery tray looks like...cool.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000004||GTFiero1||11-16-2001||11:39 PM||||i gues your a BLAZING SADDLES fan?<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||11-17-2001||11:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>Looks good.  What all are you useing off that formula?  I may need some parts for my 88 coupe!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Like the mirrors.  Sounds like fun.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>James,<P>I haven't sold anything off the car yet. Probably not going to until I'm done with the swap. <BR>The mirrors are painted red, and are not power. The car has been repainted, and I'm not sure how good the match will be with the original red. <BR>Whenever I get ready to sell parts, I'll post in the mall. There's really not much worth parting out *except* the mirrors. This thing was hit really hard. Interior was only 5 of 10. <P>Raydar<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||11-17-2001||12:01 PM||||Cheev,<BR>I'll let you know about the wrecker fee if there is one. I'm just hoping I don't have to buy a sawzall and cut it up and take it to the dump, myself.<P>Gary,<BR>The battery tray was the first thing I noticed when it was all coming apart. Looks better than either of my other Fieros. <BR>The rusty cradle bolt was on the driver's side, front. Would have been the last one I would have thought would be rusted. <BR>Although the car was packed full of Tennessee dirt-road dust.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>GTFiero1,<BR>Blazing Saddles? <BR>Yeah. But how about "Firesign Theater"? <P> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||88CoupeV6||11-17-2001||07:31 PM||||Poor car, looks like it was a nice formula at one time. <P>Ony bad thing is there are too many 88 coupe V6's now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   Copycats  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000008||fldevel||11-17-2001||10:41 PM||||hmm ..im nosey .. whats the story behind that formula .. what happend to it ?? ..i dont like to see wrecked card "especialy fieros" but i love to hear the stories behind them<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||11-18-2001||11:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88CoupeV6:<BR><B>Poor car, looks like it was a nice formula at one time. <P>Ony bad thing is there are too many 88 coupe V6's now.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   Copycats   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>...and you can take all the credit for starting the V-6 coupe trend.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>The Formula belonged to a 17(?) year old girl in Nashville. <BR>She was driving in the rain and went to make a turn. Lost traction on the wet road and parked it in a ditch. The Fiero was terminal. Don't think she had a scratch. <BR>The car had about 130,000 miles on it, but her dad told me the engine had been replaced at around 70,000.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
